 "notes": [
  "ROM/PROM substitution table: ROM 035127 at N/P3; PROM 035129 at K4, 035130 at L4, with a split pad bridged at K/L3.",
  "Revision pairs are a one-position shift: the -05/-06 board moves a designator up one row from the -01 thru -04 board (D8->D9, D9->D10, C9->C10, J8->J9). Any build must declare which revision it describes.",
  "Revision convention confirmed verbatim on the drawing: red designators are for -05/-06 assemblies; the LS174 example is F10 on -01 thru -04 and F11 on -05/-06."
 ],
 "conflicts": [
  "C8 reads as 82S129 (state-machine PROM, Atari 034002) in the state machine block and as an LS02 in the -06-only PROM block. Both cannot hold for one revision; needs resolving against a specific board.",
  "F8 is a rate multiplier on the main sheet and a 035904 PROM inside the '-06 PCB ONLY' block. The -06 section is additional circuitry, so designators there may not map onto other revisions."
 ]
